<p>W.W. Wood Products has introduced a brand-new item: the <strong>Radius End Panel</strong>, along with a <strong>full lineup of Radius Columns</strong>. Rounded ends are one of the clearest signals of the furniture-style, soft-modern look designers are asking for, and until now the usual answer was a custom shop. Not anymore.</p>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/radius-end-panel-columns/radius-end-panel-sample.webp" alt="Three views of a W.W. Wood radius end panel sample in white oak: a cutaway showing the plywood panel and solid wood quarter-round edge, and two finished views of the curved end" width="1400" height="1812" fetchpriority="high" />
</div>

<p><em>The production sample: a cutaway of the construction (left) and the finished curved end in white oak (right).</em></p>

<h2>Where they go</h2>

<p>The Radius End Panel and Radius Columns are released for:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Wall</strong> cabinets</li>
  <li><strong>Base</strong> cabinets</li>
  <li><strong>Vanity</strong> cabinets</li>
  <li><strong>Utility</strong> (tall) cabinets</li>
  <li><strong>Peninsula</strong> ends</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the sample shows</h2>

<p>The cutaway shows a plywood panel finished with a <strong>solid-wood quarter-round</strong> that forms the curve, so the radius is shaped wood rather than a bent or wrapped surface. On the finished faces, the grain carries around the curve with the rest of the panel.</p>

<h2>Where to use it</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Island and peninsula ends</strong> — the most common place a hard corner gets bumped, and the most visible place to soften the room.</li>
  <li><strong>Vanities</strong> — a radius end turns a standard vanity into a furniture piece.</li>
  <li><strong>The end of a wall run</strong> — a radius column on the last wall cabinet reads as intentional millwork, especially next to a window or open shelving.</li>
  <li><strong>Pairing:</strong> rounded ends and <a href="/playbook/pacifica-ventura-door-styles/">Pacifica's radius moulding</a> share the same soft-modern language.</li>
</ul>

